[{:db/id "q-109275/selection/0ef8964ec0a97853c9de78640006c9267484858b6037a9251f0953a6b60d7cbd" :answer/id #uuid "b4bb3f7f-3469-5405-897c-ae2bd7b7985a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "t=3\\,\\text{s}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-109275/selection/d5def0cf746ec332768f9da3bbd3918000db01e741698aca0cf711527ac7cb72" :answer/id #uuid "5b5fdd4f-b41c-552d-8974-8eaffca85c40" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "t=2\\,\\text{s}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-109275/selection/59669f0e160d1b7287db5f906150a03c8439dd8a048442ac0161f40ab8883616" :answer/id #uuid "53df5b51-d99c-5a79-819b-3a94533a12c4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "t=1\\,\\text{s}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-109275/selection/ebe8c6b8fae51c95ee0b3fb8fef6c9a7b25eb53cb5600688899d3afdc8c6f1e6" :answer/id #uuid "cc6ec469-cd59-593b-bc0a-a723d4abd25f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "t=\\frac{3}{2}\\,\\text{s}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-109275/selection/2b5c3d0f41063a46d006649b4d75b49eaa1ae58e83499d373c69c50c81bb64c0" :answer/id #uuid "713f8e69-adfe-5c71-91a2-a882cc7523a1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "t=\\frac{1}{2}\\,\\text{s}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-109275/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "b14b2892-93f5-53db-aabb-53470c6190ed" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-109275/selection/0ef8964ec0a97853c9de78640006c9267484858b6037a9251f0953a6b60d7cbd" :answer-field/choices ["q-109275/selection/0ef8964ec0a97853c9de78640006c9267484858b6037a9251f0953a6b60d7cbd" "q-109275/selection/d5def0cf746ec332768f9da3bbd3918000db01e741698aca0cf711527ac7cb72" "q-109275/selection/59669f0e160d1b7287db5f906150a03c8439dd8a048442ac0161f40ab8883616" "q-109275/selection/ebe8c6b8fae51c95ee0b3fb8fef6c9a7b25eb53cb5600688899d3afdc8c6f1e6" "q-109275/selection/2b5c3d0f41063a46d006649b4d75b49eaa1ae58e83499d373c69c50c81bb64c0"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-109275" :question/id #uuid "a2e365c2-fe58-52a7-96c4-f4db359dbf61" :question/math-academy-id "q-109275" :question/problem "The position $s(t)$ of a particle (in meters) at time $t$ seconds is given by \n\n$$\ns(t)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡({t}^{2}-6t+10),\\,t\\ge 0.\n$$\n\nCalculate the time at which the particle is stationary." :question/worked-solution "The particle is stationary when its velocity is zero. So first, we need to calculate the velocity function. We can do that by taking the derivative of the position function, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}s}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡({t}^{2}-6t+10)) \\\\  & =\\frac{2t-6}{{t}^{2}-6t+10} \\\\  & =\\frac{2(t-3)}{{t}^{2}-6t+10}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe particle is stationary when $v=0\\,\\text{m/s}.$ So, we set $v=0$ and solve for $t:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2(t-3)}{{t}^{2}-6t+10} & =0 \\\\ 2(t-3) & =0 \\\\ t & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the particle is stationary at $t=3\\,\\text{s}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-109275/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e21f194e-fb5d-5c90-af38-18d8c75582a9"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-109275"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-109274/selection/d5def0cf746ec332768f9da3bbd3918000db01e741698aca0cf711527ac7cb72" :answer/id #uuid "59bf99a4-4487-5b03-b2c0-5ba248cdffc5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "t=2\\,\\text{s}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-109274/selection/aec6edb53cb2fc502ab3737374ed30718b6fe084c86f2a6c8d026096cd9f70dc" :answer/id #uuid "4b609f51-6620-5550-84a4-565df43107d8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "t=3{e}^{2}\\,\\text{s}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-109274/selection/ebe8c6b8fae51c95ee0b3fb8fef6c9a7b25eb53cb5600688899d3afdc8c6f1e6" :answer/id #uuid "49a8aa83-c4a2-589e-842a-b85f4529b97f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "t=\\frac{3}{2}\\,\\text{s}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-109274/selection/0ef8964ec0a97853c9de78640006c9267484858b6037a9251f0953a6b60d7cbd" :answer/id #uuid "c8cd8a91-5381-568a-bbfe-1f703ad6407d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "t=3\\,\\text{s}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-109274/selection/9fdff1cd89b1def20170bc5af243d28fe043e68d43933bc513d1e97f3dd6f104" :answer/id #uuid "b40340f9-c466-514f-884a-2e7d7b67a2de" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "t=2{e}^{2}\\,\\text{s}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-109274/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "35640171-26d5-56b7-8531-903070905429" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-109274/selection/d5def0cf746ec332768f9da3bbd3918000db01e741698aca0cf711527ac7cb72" :answer-field/choices ["q-109274/selection/d5def0cf746ec332768f9da3bbd3918000db01e741698aca0cf711527ac7cb72" "q-109274/selection/aec6edb53cb2fc502ab3737374ed30718b6fe084c86f2a6c8d026096cd9f70dc" "q-109274/selection/ebe8c6b8fae51c95ee0b3fb8fef6c9a7b25eb53cb5600688899d3afdc8c6f1e6" "q-109274/selection/0ef8964ec0a97853c9de78640006c9267484858b6037a9251f0953a6b60d7cbd" "q-109274/selection/9fdff1cd89b1def20170bc5af243d28fe043e68d43933bc513d1e97f3dd6f104"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-109274" :question/id #uuid "25e83974-7897-5d7f-96f2-7e49663e3f50" :question/math-academy-id "q-109274" :question/problem "The position $s(t)$ of a particle (in meters) at time $t$ seconds is given by \n\n$$\ns(t)=(t-3){e}^{t},\\,t\\ge 0.\n$$\n\nCalculate the time at which the particle is stationary." :question/worked-solution "The particle is stationary when its velocity is zero. So first, we need to calculate the velocity function. We can do that by taking the derivative of the position function, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}s}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}((t-3){e}^{t}) \\\\  & ={e}^{t}+(t-3){e}^{t} \\\\  & =(t-2){e}^{t}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe particle is stationary when $v=0\\,\\text{m/s}.$ So, we set $v=0$ and solve for $t:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(t-2){e}^{t} & =0 \\\\ t-2 & =0 \\\\ t & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the particle is stationary at $t=2\\,\\text{s}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-109274/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e21f194e-fb5d-5c90-af38-18d8c75582a9"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-109274"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-4771/selection/20b7bbf47e4159d425683ef96d3217c51e3972c1a9f75a41eff076cb46db14cf" :answer/id #uuid "0a8c6717-d882-5d52-a491-71cffae3080e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "t=8\\,\\text{s}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-4771/selection/f232b2e21fa38e5671736495c79c8df9c368a8623cbe81147c1e4f08daca2644" :answer/id #uuid "dfe38831-2ebc-538b-a2c2-50cfd4926f08" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "t=10\\,\\text{s}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-4771/selection/d5def0cf746ec332768f9da3bbd3918000db01e741698aca0cf711527ac7cb72" :answer/id #uuid "ec27b930-4e71-59aa-b104-86b82ce1b543" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "t=2\\,\\text{s}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-4771/selection/1ed310c568129094bb708a92e64aac05e57d915c64a6116702028f8effd7d987" :answer/id #uuid "c528b48f-fdbf-5397-b017-50d5926ff5c3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "t=7\\,\\text{s}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-4771/selection/ba771dd41a37fcd1cabd147925488b8d4a7729bdbd79040a1a290ed8e3379a45" :answer/id #uuid "0bfa9dab-4042-5177-b960-f74d772f577f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "t=5\\,\\text{s}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-4771/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "d05e1821-bf10-52dd-b786-afb9afa67640" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-4771/selection/ba771dd41a37fcd1cabd147925488b8d4a7729bdbd79040a1a290ed8e3379a45" :answer-field/choices ["q-4771/selection/20b7bbf47e4159d425683ef96d3217c51e3972c1a9f75a41eff076cb46db14cf" "q-4771/selection/f232b2e21fa38e5671736495c79c8df9c368a8623cbe81147c1e4f08daca2644" "q-4771/selection/d5def0cf746ec332768f9da3bbd3918000db01e741698aca0cf711527ac7cb72" "q-4771/selection/1ed310c568129094bb708a92e64aac05e57d915c64a6116702028f8effd7d987" "q-4771/selection/ba771dd41a37fcd1cabd147925488b8d4a7729bdbd79040a1a290ed8e3379a45"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-4771" :question/id #uuid "24413cc5-0267-5920-b89f-10f793534ebf" :question/math-academy-id "q-4771" :question/problem "The position $x(t)$ of a particle (in meters) at time $t$ seconds is given by \n\n$$\nx(t)={t}^{2}-10t-2,\\,t\\ge 0.\n$$\n\nCalculate the time at which the particle is stationary." :question/worked-solution "First, we need to calculate the velocity function. We can do that by taking the derivative of the position function, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2}-10t-2) \\\\  & =2t-10\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe particle is stationary when $v=0\\,\\text{m/s}.$ So, we set $v=0$ and solve for $t:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2t-10 & =0 \\\\ 2t & =10 \\\\ t & =5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the particle is stationary at $t=5\\,\\text{s}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-4771/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e21f194e-fb5d-5c90-af38-18d8c75582a9"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-4771"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-73188/selection/68403c81963fa3241683eb5e7810d9fe3ccf698d8ad53cd333e1238d0e58f02f" :answer/id #uuid "64a51385-11d7-51c7-a2d4-7659fb60ca51" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "t=2,\\,s=8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73188/selection/c57f90c68f091755d1fe4e90ea6dfc98421b44cf2334d7d512c519030cefc85a" :answer/id #uuid "9ceb25f5-097c-520e-aaf4-5ab806fd9f50" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "t=3,\\,s=11" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73188/selection/fb0f43bf76f3be80bd735c38e7908802f359e0beddcdc05958501cc6bc5de409" :answer/id #uuid "7b258107-4669-57fb-b219-823bab2c3396" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "t=1,\\,s=10" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73188/selection/c8145cb550d367ea40aa9617c28e406ddd6e4dbcc98c524392ededee6829b98c" :answer/id #uuid "55b41eab-0494-56bc-92fe-c4dd35e7ce67" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "t=1,\\,s=7" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73188/selection/7d54b1d8ebc720650fd7d132e1cefad536918c191b298c239fe2cd4c2243b99b" :answer/id #uuid "e5251bd4-427b-5273-8a5d-2b9528d5d26b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "t=3,\\,s=9" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73188/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "a8d351ef-39f4-5dae-94d8-3aeaa48f46a4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-73188/selection/c8145cb550d367ea40aa9617c28e406ddd6e4dbcc98c524392ededee6829b98c" :answer-field/choices ["q-73188/selection/68403c81963fa3241683eb5e7810d9fe3ccf698d8ad53cd333e1238d0e58f02f" "q-73188/selection/c57f90c68f091755d1fe4e90ea6dfc98421b44cf2334d7d512c519030cefc85a" "q-73188/selection/fb0f43bf76f3be80bd735c38e7908802f359e0beddcdc05958501cc6bc5de409" "q-73188/selection/c8145cb550d367ea40aa9617c28e406ddd6e4dbcc98c524392ededee6829b98c" "q-73188/selection/7d54b1d8ebc720650fd7d132e1cefad536918c191b298c239fe2cd4c2243b99b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-73188" :question/id #uuid "a2ee9a7a-96f8-5c1a-98bc-31a0726aad61" :question/math-academy-id "q-73188" :question/problem "The position $s(t)$ of a particle at time $t$ is given by \n\n$$\ns(t)={t}^{2}-2t+8,\\,t\\ge 0.\n$$\n\nCalculate the time when the particle is stationary, and give the displacement of the particle from the origin at this time." :question/worked-solution "The particle is stationary when its velocity is zero. So first, we need to calculate the velocity function. We can do that by taking the derivative of the position function, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}s}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2}-2t+8) \\\\  & =2t-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe particle is stationary when $v=0$ So, we set $v=0$ and solve for $t:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2t-2 & =0 \\\\ 2t & =2 \\\\ t & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo the particle is stationary only at $t=1.$ To find the displacement from the origin at this time, we substitute $t=1$ back into $s(t)$ and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}s(1) & ={1}^{2}-2(1)+8 \\\\  & =1-2+8 \\\\  & =7.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the particle is stationary at $t=1$ and its displacement from the origin at this time is $7.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-73188/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e21f194e-fb5d-5c90-af38-18d8c75582a9"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-73188"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-109276/selection/e3529c5097809598f64063bcc942331aecc2d81cd8b03b4f4745066798f1cc8a" :answer/id #uuid "846c852f-b19d-5eb0-9c5f-6a43fa64007d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "t=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{e}}\\,\\text{s}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-109276/selection/7b83b1e95c83c5331f3bcd8ddf7343b45a7a2f21b360f802c825a067915477b6" :answer/id #uuid "1b591117-c147-5078-bb26-0bc06b59aa5a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "t=e\\,\\text{s}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-109276/selection/bd687bb4e4f64a9842e926df173c3771dec548739debafa30b50d59811d90e60" :answer/id #uuid "91f98767-8bd1-536f-9465-8fe19115b782" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "t=\\sqrt{e}\\,\\text{s}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-109276/selection/59669f0e160d1b7287db5f906150a03c8439dd8a048442ac0161f40ab8883616" :answer/id #uuid "a21dfbdd-deb0-5415-a30b-f58eaa37838a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "t=1\\,\\text{s}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-109276/selection/d0fdbee5ef2f1c1f510b6c8d66ce615215938073dc06d31be8f870d5060a1fa8" :answer/id #uuid "cbcbc8b2-e2e2-5466-a60b-ff17c0cc6836" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "t=\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{e}}\\,\\text{s}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-109276/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "3130adfc-ef2a-5b80-b47c-71c848fca0b3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-109276/selection/e3529c5097809598f64063bcc942331aecc2d81cd8b03b4f4745066798f1cc8a" :answer-field/choices ["q-109276/selection/e3529c5097809598f64063bcc942331aecc2d81cd8b03b4f4745066798f1cc8a" "q-109276/selection/7b83b1e95c83c5331f3bcd8ddf7343b45a7a2f21b360f802c825a067915477b6" "q-109276/selection/bd687bb4e4f64a9842e926df173c3771dec548739debafa30b50d59811d90e60" "q-109276/selection/59669f0e160d1b7287db5f906150a03c8439dd8a048442ac0161f40ab8883616" "q-109276/selection/d0fdbee5ef2f1c1f510b6c8d66ce615215938073dc06d31be8f870d5060a1fa8"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-109276" :question/id #uuid "d098c0db-a314-5213-9701-dea3457fb68f" :question/math-academy-id "q-109276" :question/problem "The position $s(t)$ of a particle (in meters) at time $t$ seconds is given by \n\n$$\ns(t)={t}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t,\\,t>0.\n$$\n\nCalculate the time at which the particle is stationary." :question/worked-solution "The particle is stationary when its velocity is zero. So first, we need to calculate the velocity function. We can do that by taking the derivative of the position function, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}s}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t) \\\\  & =2t\\operatorname{ln}⁡t+{t}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{t} \\\\  & =2t\\operatorname{ln}⁡t+t \\\\  & =t(2\\operatorname{ln}⁡t+1)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe particle is stationary when $v=0\\,\\text{m/s}.$ So, we set $v=0$ and solve for $t:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}t(2\\operatorname{ln}⁡t+1) & =0 \\\\ 2\\operatorname{ln}⁡t+1 & =0 \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡t & =-\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ t & ={e}^{-1/2} \\\\ t & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{e}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the particle is stationary at $t=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{e}}\\,\\text{s}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-109276/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e21f194e-fb5d-5c90-af38-18d8c75582a9"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-109276"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-48912/selection/777e8eb0b47756d164247cb94188ad40db7b4909b9f10dc4e76d26f8f7d72712" :answer/id #uuid "a58f6864-c59b-5bdc-b124-ec8f5452cad1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(4,\\infty )" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-48912/selection/f83a49ac29e3ff7d2e54628a1541251461a6d0aac474ca54d39bf792f176b350" :answer/id #uuid "3b6afbe4-d16e-5d05-9fc4-d7aab17e979a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[0,\\frac{5}{6})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-48912/selection/cf3808444b4fa968ba3db45c6d31c1974b033318f837d957f26b7452ad082bec" :answer/id #uuid "21a8c3c8-b06e-51dc-8f8f-6f18677bbf62" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(2,\\frac{13}{4})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-48912/selection/a2d296cb9b30f36c87ab3145c1c37682f0bba39f1773cc0cbe90eca09a281cf3" :answer/id #uuid "fee1eebf-f311-55a9-9222-2595f1919cf7" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$[0,\\frac{5}{3})$ and $(\\frac{7}{2},\\infty )$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-48912/selection/2c171b1ced074e1bf653a6512065e4f4433f85d922f78f3b6c3ef2c2c4662912" :answer/id #uuid "23b1fbde-50c2-5d53-b5a1-85d5f81fba1f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(\\frac{3}{4},\\infty )" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-48912/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "7b20ae87-2caa-5a0e-81f0-bb93426cd586" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-48912/selection/2c171b1ced074e1bf653a6512065e4f4433f85d922f78f3b6c3ef2c2c4662912" :answer-field/choices ["q-48912/selection/777e8eb0b47756d164247cb94188ad40db7b4909b9f10dc4e76d26f8f7d72712" "q-48912/selection/f83a49ac29e3ff7d2e54628a1541251461a6d0aac474ca54d39bf792f176b350" "q-48912/selection/cf3808444b4fa968ba3db45c6d31c1974b033318f837d957f26b7452ad082bec" "q-48912/selection/a2d296cb9b30f36c87ab3145c1c37682f0bba39f1773cc0cbe90eca09a281cf3" "q-48912/selection/2c171b1ced074e1bf653a6512065e4f4433f85d922f78f3b6c3ef2c2c4662912"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-48912" :question/id #uuid "bc288872-1b0f-5431-bcdb-4e1ae6d59811" :question/math-academy-id "q-48912" :question/problem "The displacement $s$ (in meters) relative to a fixed origin $O$ of a particle moving in a straight line along the $x$-axis is given by $s(t)=(4t-7){e}^{t}$, where $t\\ge 0$ is the time measured in seconds. Determine the time intervals in which the particle is moving in the direction of increasing $x.$" :question/worked-solution "If the particle moves in the direction of increasing $x,$ then its velocity is positive.\n\nFirst, we calculate the velocity function by differentiating the position function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}s}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}((4t-7){e}^{t}) \\\\  & =(4t-3){e}^{t}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo calculate time intervals in which the particle is moving in the direction of increasing $x$, we solve $v(t)>0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & >0 \\\\ (4t-3){e}^{t} & >0 \\\\ 4t-3 & >0 \\\\ t & >\\frac{3}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the time interval in which the particle is moving to the direction of increasing $x$ is $(\\frac{3}{4},\\infty ).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-48912/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f8f3989e-bde0-5b3a-8d45-08f34d330c3f"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-48912"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-48911/selection/d15e7963bdd9eb5577b6a9b885d9df314c603957d625ef545317c7f8a3165d18" :answer/id #uuid "a066c75f-3bc7-51a4-8343-3ad5b2be2feb" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$[0,1)$ and $(2,+\\infty )$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-48911/selection/784b37f7a414987e21224ca3fffda9176023cbdd0d8508d7b9bdb18ed8b8d069" :answer/id #uuid "38fc2c1d-45af-5e1c-aaa8-aa3aef0a9c45" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[0,2)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-48911/selection/4f6dd30811e3d9b72aa44fe39d96aa66ade8028e718323bb69c5e1cd5500d589" :answer/id #uuid "516e0e63-71c6-55ed-97c4-7de922ca8d6c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(2,+\\infty )" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-48911/selection/80fdd79931a564cbe8cda0116a1645a581b63abe3cc6ee3b38561998c052cbda" :answer/id #uuid "fb1f4886-e014-579a-85eb-ab6560fee7d9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(3,4)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-48911/selection/804d402f0d1aeb287543f7a51842b28febac022a74c358f4b99f4c9c8164987f" :answer/id #uuid "0e0a6517-4be9-5455-8d1e-f73ee43cab39" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$(1,2)$ and $(4,8)$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-48911/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "966fbba2-e395-5db4-80cc-399e442cbf30" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-48911/selection/784b37f7a414987e21224ca3fffda9176023cbdd0d8508d7b9bdb18ed8b8d069" :answer-field/choices ["q-48911/selection/d15e7963bdd9eb5577b6a9b885d9df314c603957d625ef545317c7f8a3165d18" "q-48911/selection/784b37f7a414987e21224ca3fffda9176023cbdd0d8508d7b9bdb18ed8b8d069" "q-48911/selection/4f6dd30811e3d9b72aa44fe39d96aa66ade8028e718323bb69c5e1cd5500d589" "q-48911/selection/80fdd79931a564cbe8cda0116a1645a581b63abe3cc6ee3b38561998c052cbda" "q-48911/selection/804d402f0d1aeb287543f7a51842b28febac022a74c358f4b99f4c9c8164987f"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-48911" :question/id #uuid "3c0cff5d-5154-58d2-b27e-3d3d4bba184f" :question/math-academy-id "q-48911" :question/problem "The displacement $s$ (in meters) relative to a fixed origin $O$ of a particle moving in a straight line along the $x$-axis is given by $s(t)={e}^{{t}^{2}-4t+6}$, where $t\\ge 0$ is the time measured in seconds. Find the time intervals in which the particle is moving in the direction of decreasing $x.$" :question/worked-solution "If the particle moves in the direction of decreasing $x,$ then its velocity is negative.\n\nFirst, we calculate the velocity function by differentiating the position function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}s}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{{t}^{2}-4t+6}) \\\\  & =(2t-4){e}^{{t}^{2}-4t+6}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo calculate time intervals in which the particle is moving in the direction of decreasing $x$, we must solve $v(t)<0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & <0 \\\\ (2t-4){e}^{{t}^{2}-4t+6} & <0 \\\\ 2t-4 & <0 \\\\ 2t & <4 \\\\ t & <2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the time interval in which the particle is moving to the direction of decreasing $x$ is $[0,2).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-48911/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f8f3989e-bde0-5b3a-8d45-08f34d330c3f"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-48911"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-335891/field-1/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "2e13c911-464c-5d7f-8dcd-8a6399f99780" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-335891/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "16c17a4d-4139-5a95-bd2c-8dcaaaf8d895" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-335891/field-1/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer-field/choices ["q-335891/field-1/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-335891/field-2/b67476ffce451bf9cc94e82f22f7f4f4b23075d2e02b9ea63c2ad56fd611692c" :answer/id #uuid "4abb84c0-11c0-517e-990b-238a48e3c5a0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\infty" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-335891/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "2890d096-a837-580f-a80b-fcad1fdec5ef" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-335891/field-2/b67476ffce451bf9cc94e82f22f7f4f4b23075d2e02b9ea63c2ad56fd611692c" :answer-field/choices ["q-335891/field-2/b67476ffce451bf9cc94e82f22f7f4f4b23075d2e02b9ea63c2ad56fd611692c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-335891" :question/id #uuid "92d00e03-01ad-583d-a312-9474b7c65d31" :question/math-academy-id "q-335891" :question/problem "The displacement $s,$ in meters, relative to a fixed origin $O$ of a particle moving in a straight line along the $x$-axis is given by $s(t)=\\sqrt{5{t}^{2}-20t+29},$ where $t>0$ is the time, measured in seconds. Find the time intervals in which the particle is moving in the direction of increasing $x.$\n\n$t\\in (${{field-1}},\n\n{{field-2}}$)$" :question/worked-solution "If the particle moves in the direction of increasing $x,$ then its velocity is positive. \n\nFirst, we calculate the velocity function by differentiating the position function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}s}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\sqrt{5{t}^{2}-20t+29}) \\\\  & =\\frac{10t-20}{2\\sqrt{5{t}^{2}-20t+29}} \\\\  & =\\frac{10(t-2)}{2\\sqrt{5{t}^{2}-20t+29}} \\\\  & =\\frac{5(t-2)}{\\sqrt{5{t}^{2}-20t+29}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo calculate time intervals in which the particle is moving in the direction of increasing $x$, we solve $v(t)>0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & >0 \\\\ \\frac{5(t-2)}{\\sqrt{5{t}^{2}-20t+29}} & >0 \\\\ 5(t-2) & >0 \\\\ t-2 & >0 \\\\ t & >2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the time interval in which the particle is moving to the direction of increasing $x$ is \n\n$$\nt\\in (2,\\infty ).\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-335891/field-1" "q-335891/field-2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f8f3989e-bde0-5b3a-8d45-08f34d330c3f"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-335891"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-73210/selection/125a139eea2f35d78cb434c2a4858d0e0f07baa12b39859b72b588bce172ec2b" :answer/id #uuid "27c75026-69c0-5fd1-931c-66bcbf46941e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[0,\\frac{1}{4})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73210/selection/666f053dfd67b80d5f1d4eabcffa4615b3cd8e35d21d597b800599704fd5f9bc" :answer/id #uuid "36b83a65-b648-5c45-964c-a215cbb65863" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[0,1)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73210/selection/502f17636638d27e20cc4ce83769b10cc10a93be28b7908fa4422eb7e7ae9ac2" :answer/id #uuid "24e3583f-547f-5fd4-a804-1deccb1ec905" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(\\frac{1}{2},\\infty )" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73210/selection/aa9e66fc87813ce6fe39267b051b8bbea4fe75e382b4d473683ad4d47d1c5f6f" :answer/id #uuid "c5d034a0-68f3-5d2b-988f-e11655a10068" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(\\frac{1}{4},\\infty )" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73210/selection/9d1976cda7c4bf5635995714e3f54e71e97af4aa6204fcc11f9644b182022263" :answer/id #uuid "b30f0709-5e9b-57ba-b7eb-3c77da20fffc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[0,\\frac{1}{2})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73210/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "adf9aa9a-aa1a-51c7-baeb-c45e3854e95c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-73210/selection/9d1976cda7c4bf5635995714e3f54e71e97af4aa6204fcc11f9644b182022263" :answer-field/choices ["q-73210/selection/125a139eea2f35d78cb434c2a4858d0e0f07baa12b39859b72b588bce172ec2b" "q-73210/selection/666f053dfd67b80d5f1d4eabcffa4615b3cd8e35d21d597b800599704fd5f9bc" "q-73210/selection/502f17636638d27e20cc4ce83769b10cc10a93be28b7908fa4422eb7e7ae9ac2" "q-73210/selection/aa9e66fc87813ce6fe39267b051b8bbea4fe75e382b4d473683ad4d47d1c5f6f" "q-73210/selection/9d1976cda7c4bf5635995714e3f54e71e97af4aa6204fcc11f9644b182022263"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-73210" :question/id #uuid "08503449-abde-5746-b6d7-46180193efed" :question/math-academy-id "q-73210" :question/problem "The displacement $s,$ in meters, relative to a fixed origin $O$ of a particle moving in a straight line along the $x$-axis is given by $s(t)=t{e}^{-2t}$, where $t\\ge 0$ is the time, measured in seconds. Find the time intervals in which the particle is moving in the direction of increasing $x.$" :question/worked-solution "If the particle moves in the direction of increasing $x,$ then its velocity is positive. \n\nFirst, we calculate the velocity function by differentiating the position function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}s}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t{e}^{-2t}) \\\\  & ={e}^{-2t}(1-2t)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo calculate time intervals in which the particle is moving in the direction of increasing $x$, we solve $v(t)>0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & >0 \\\\ {e}^{-2t}(1-2t) & >0 \\\\ 1-2t & >0 \\\\ 2t & <1 \\\\ t & <\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the time interval in which the particle is moving to the direction of increasing $x$ is $t\\in [0,\\frac{1}{2}).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-73210/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f8f3989e-bde0-5b3a-8d45-08f34d330c3f"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-73210"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-315550/field-1/b93157e0eb36ec8e645eeabaa0819400f448209e0db24c1abf59704822466393" :answer/id #uuid "dd79ef94-fcdf-58f6-aa30-5aa511cb311b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-315550/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "21660576-1240-5665-a5f3-e25ef9579462" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-315550/field-1/b93157e0eb36ec8e645eeabaa0819400f448209e0db24c1abf59704822466393" :answer-field/choices ["q-315550/field-1/b93157e0eb36ec8e645eeabaa0819400f448209e0db24c1abf59704822466393"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-315550/field-2/b67476ffce451bf9cc94e82f22f7f4f4b23075d2e02b9ea63c2ad56fd611692c" :answer/id #uuid "2110c1da-b1a4-56c2-839d-ec6245598cd9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\infty" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-315550/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "45b0bf94-741a-59b3-b780-9aa3ef6a0c61" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-315550/field-2/b67476ffce451bf9cc94e82f22f7f4f4b23075d2e02b9ea63c2ad56fd611692c" :answer-field/choices ["q-315550/field-2/b67476ffce451bf9cc94e82f22f7f4f4b23075d2e02b9ea63c2ad56fd611692c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-315550" :question/id #uuid "c26d8c3c-e107-52ba-89a9-ccc2af1eaed1" :question/math-academy-id "q-315550" :question/problem "The displacement $s,$ in meters, relative to a fixed origin $O$ of a particle moving in a straight line along the $x$-axis is given by $s(t)=(4t-7){e}^{t},$ where $t>0$ is the time, measured in seconds. Find the time intervals in which the particle is moving in the direction of increasing $x.$\n\n$t\\in (${{field-1}},\n\n{{field-2}}$)$" :question/worked-solution "If the particle moves in the direction of increasing $x,$ then its velocity is positive. \n\nFirst, we calculate the velocity function by differentiating the position function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}s}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}((4t-7){e}^{t}) \\\\  & =4{e}^{t}+(4t-7){e}^{t} \\\\  & =(4t-3){e}^{t}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo calculate time intervals in which the particle is moving in the direction of increasing $x$, we solve $v(t)>0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & >0 \\\\ (4t-3){e}^{t} & >0 \\\\ 4t-3 & >0 \\\\ t & >\\frac{3}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the time interval in which the particle is moving to the direction of increasing $x$ is \n\n$$\nt\\in (\\frac{3}{4},\\infty ).\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-315550/field-1" "q-315550/field-2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f8f3989e-bde0-5b3a-8d45-08f34d330c3f"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-315550"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-109303/selection/f5fe4de4627e8b971cbbf82cdd6f169c9abf5bbb198e82a0730b5a07a349819c" :answer/id #uuid "3797d18a-9760-5eed-b498-d2249d5f5bef" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "t=2,\\,v=-\\frac{11}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-109303/selection/377e35e98275f0d369e56b7860e22c341ef0e6120f545f11aa825e686b2d5b50" :answer/id #uuid "07ed0936-e17d-56a2-839c-782eb9417875" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "t=4,\\,v=6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-109303/selection/4eb7b19cd6f3f5bb65141976a196f228d6d7b4fd892907948b94a63a2a41ca98" :answer/id #uuid "8fb12910-836c-5ee3-a2d4-8227b04bd969" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "t=1,\\,v=\\frac{7}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-109303/selection/9bc7a95f4520e3af7c60b677a6dc8b54191af68d1d44f88c3e1a62f884a4d683" :answer/id #uuid "8e6707f7-9d76-52fc-9d3a-9585efc9456b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "t=4,\\,v=-4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-109303/selection/0d38133ea93ee90ba2d48d92b536e039a630f73de57bb17c275661009ebded8f" :answer/id #uuid "bbf2036c-e6a0-56af-9ea3-9f5e80a00d48" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "t=2,\\,v=8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-109303/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "b2b6a8bf-a6eb-53f0-87b5-74af3210b40e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-109303/selection/377e35e98275f0d369e56b7860e22c341ef0e6120f545f11aa825e686b2d5b50" :answer-field/choices ["q-109303/selection/f5fe4de4627e8b971cbbf82cdd6f169c9abf5bbb198e82a0730b5a07a349819c" "q-109303/selection/377e35e98275f0d369e56b7860e22c341ef0e6120f545f11aa825e686b2d5b50" "q-109303/selection/4eb7b19cd6f3f5bb65141976a196f228d6d7b4fd892907948b94a63a2a41ca98" "q-109303/selection/9bc7a95f4520e3af7c60b677a6dc8b54191af68d1d44f88c3e1a62f884a4d683" "q-109303/selection/0d38133ea93ee90ba2d48d92b536e039a630f73de57bb17c275661009ebded8f"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-109303" :question/id #uuid "9c55e4cb-31ae-5f26-9005-765720eabd10" :question/math-academy-id "q-109303" :question/problem "A particle $P$ is traveling along the $x$-axis with displacement $s(t)$ from a fixed origin $O$ given by\n\n$$\ns(t)=\\frac{{t}^{3}}{2}-6{t}^{2}+30t+4,\\,t\\ge 0.\n$$\n\nFind the time at which the acceleration is zero, and find the value of the velocity at this moment." :question/worked-solution "First, we calculate $v(t)$ by differentiating $s(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}s}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{{t}^{3}}{2}-6{t}^{2}+30t+4) \\\\  & =\\frac{3{t}^{2}}{2}-12t+30\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we differentiate $v(t)$ to find $a(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{3{t}^{2}}{2}-12t+30) \\\\  & =3t-12\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we put $a=0$ to find the time when the acceleration is zero:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3t-12 & =0 \\\\ 3t & =12 \\\\ t & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the acceleration is zero when $t=4.$ To find the velocity at this moment, we substitute this back into $v(t)$ to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(4) & =\\frac{3(4)^{2}}{2}-12(4)+30 \\\\  & =24-48+30 \\\\  & =6\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-109303/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "bee6d4bf-79da-5eb3-a214-8c045dbce5bd"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-109303"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-7188/selection/82e8313fbcb1cbd4b7f06a4101df7cf8454a2cfa0c685321f455d3d60b74c8e0" :answer/id #uuid "6c794664-d4be-5c42-8d2e-8b38f7bc2221" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "t=4.5,\\,v=12" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-7188/selection/5095687fe3fb13203efb8610b1aba0dec3fb778e9a685893f2e20cce309ba72b" :answer/id #uuid "74745f3f-0369-5e06-ae45-e46284728b6b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "t=4.5,\\,v=27.5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-7188/selection/292583bd58d8d31063c0d81cd737b1ea3321d89a712b0a7ae3cff91bd0f65d39" :answer/id #uuid "559aca53-c76f-5fe2-9796-05e478a143a4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "t=4,\\,v=10.75" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-7188/selection/da348106fb6ab9beb2fc07e1ae161c125ec11c7b19909075d71740ba88a14e7f" :answer/id #uuid "a4f415dc-47c2-5c64-8808-2e0040849906" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "t=4,\\,v=22.5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-7188/selection/b50cdd35ed5a2ab763b466b0c97ddb13721e512fe5f0012964c046d502989b80" :answer/id #uuid "029a872a-a5b9-50b1-855f-8c9f9a283eef" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "t=3.5,\\,v=26.5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-7188/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "5b117898-dfe1-5e92-bcc9-e5e138747efe" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-7188/selection/5095687fe3fb13203efb8610b1aba0dec3fb778e9a685893f2e20cce309ba72b" :answer-field/choices ["q-7188/selection/82e8313fbcb1cbd4b7f06a4101df7cf8454a2cfa0c685321f455d3d60b74c8e0" "q-7188/selection/5095687fe3fb13203efb8610b1aba0dec3fb778e9a685893f2e20cce309ba72b" "q-7188/selection/292583bd58d8d31063c0d81cd737b1ea3321d89a712b0a7ae3cff91bd0f65d39" "q-7188/selection/da348106fb6ab9beb2fc07e1ae161c125ec11c7b19909075d71740ba88a14e7f" "q-7188/selection/b50cdd35ed5a2ab763b466b0c97ddb13721e512fe5f0012964c046d502989b80"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-7188" :question/id #uuid "e823f661-78ed-5c49-931f-9f7b092bd2fe" :question/math-academy-id "q-7188" :question/problem "A particle $P$ is traveling along the $x$-axis with displacement $s(t)$ from a fixed origin $O$ given by\n\n$$\ns(t)=-\\frac{2}{9}{t}^{3}+3{t}^{2}+14t+17,\\,t\\ge 0.\n$$\n\nFind the time at which the acceleration is zero, and find the value of the velocity at this moment." :question/worked-solution "First, we calculate $v(t)$ by differentiating $s(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}s}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(-\\frac{2}{9}{t}^{3}+3{t}^{2}+14t+17) \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{3}{t}^{2}+6t+14\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nNow, we differentiate $v(t)$ to find $a(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(-\\frac{2}{3}{t}^{2}+6t+14) \\\\  & =-\\frac{4}{3}t+6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we put $a=0$ to find the time when the acceleration is zero:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}0 & =-\\frac{4}{3}t+6 \\\\ \\frac{4}{3}t & =6 \\\\ t & =4.5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo the acceleration is zero when $t=4.5.$ To find the velocity at this moment, we substitute this back into $v(t)$ to get\n\n$$\nv(4.5)=-\\frac{2}{3}(4.5)^{2}+6(4.5)+14=27.5.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-7188/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "bee6d4bf-79da-5eb3-a214-8c045dbce5bd"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-7188"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-73334"] :question/problem "A particle $P$ is traveling along the $x$-axis with displacement $s(t)$ from a fixed origin $O$ given by\n\n$$\ns(t)={t}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(t),\\,t\\ge 0.\n$$\n\nFind the time at which the acceleration is zero, and find the value of the velocity at this moment." :question/worked-solution "First, we calculate $v(t)$ by differentiating $s(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}s}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(t)) \\\\  & =2t\\operatorname{ln}⁡(t)+t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nNow, we differentiate $v(t)$ to find $a(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t+2t\\operatorname{ln}⁡(t)) \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{ln}⁡(t)+3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we put $a=0$ to find the time when the acceleration is zero:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}0 & =2\\operatorname{ln}⁡(t)+3 \\\\ 2\\operatorname{ln}⁡(t) & =-3 \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡(t) & =-\\frac{3}{2} \\\\ t & ={e}^{-3/2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo the acceleration is zero when $t={e}^{-3/2}.$ To find the velocity at this moment, we substitute this back into $v(t)$ to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v({e}^{-3/2}) & =2({e}^{-3/2})\\operatorname{ln}⁡({e}^{-3/2})+{e}^{-3/2} \\\\  & =2{e}^{-3/2}(-\\frac{3}{2})+{e}^{-3/2} \\\\  & =-2{e}^{-3/2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-109302/selection/7fcd4e40d9ca7a966f312f2a3ea3422aa82aea0b3b5dcb5c9500ac99950653f1" :answer/id #uuid "cf33ce5c-8b17-5a2b-b843-cd05b9188fb6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "t=1,\\,v=-7" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-109302/selection/cfa8a9b3821bc60e73b26f3ad51514d788701f2f1e4dbb4bfad529a618a417e8" :answer/id #uuid "36244f2c-51b5-5da6-861d-f5d5cf3e1a54" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "t=\\frac{1}{2},\\,v=-\\frac{8}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-109302/selection/448aaac4257ba74e3edc51b0fd83ae4d97f4c38b0762bfdc8b3e9d9ca4601aea" :answer/id #uuid "de7a8620-0953-5a2a-99bd-578e05b45ce2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "t=1,\\,v=\\frac{15}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-109302/selection/79c7a20049285b0b8c987bbd357d3aba1ae7e1ee6b80dddc74c3fea0a01f1c0f" :answer/id #uuid "bd259a28-0f07-56f4-99b3-cc005d451f06" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "t=\\frac{3}{2},\\,v=-\\frac{21}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-109302/selection/bd0fa00db7408e6c7239530701317372ca1efd97b5283bec47d8e5021ccf2522" :answer/id #uuid "9aaa5172-9aef-55df-9812-6f0aa569256a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "t=\\frac{3}{2},\\,v=9" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-109302/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "7dc3cc59-7e89-5c2c-824f-cbadf0f09f87" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-109302/selection/79c7a20049285b0b8c987bbd357d3aba1ae7e1ee6b80dddc74c3fea0a01f1c0f" :answer-field/choices ["q-109302/selection/7fcd4e40d9ca7a966f312f2a3ea3422aa82aea0b3b5dcb5c9500ac99950653f1" "q-109302/selection/cfa8a9b3821bc60e73b26f3ad51514d788701f2f1e4dbb4bfad529a618a417e8" "q-109302/selection/448aaac4257ba74e3edc51b0fd83ae4d97f4c38b0762bfdc8b3e9d9ca4601aea" "q-109302/selection/79c7a20049285b0b8c987bbd357d3aba1ae7e1ee6b80dddc74c3fea0a01f1c0f" "q-109302/selection/bd0fa00db7408e6c7239530701317372ca1efd97b5283bec47d8e5021ccf2522"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-109302" :question/id #uuid "6414dac4-9443-5e38-b246-ae2ca315e478" :question/math-academy-id "q-109302" :question/problem "A particle $P$ is traveling along the $x$-axis with displacement $s(t)$ from a fixed origin $O$ given by\n\n$$\ns(t)=2{t}^{3}-9{t}^{2}+3t-2,\\,t\\ge 0.\n$$\n\nFind the time at which the acceleration is zero, and find the value of the velocity at this moment." :question/worked-solution "First, we calculate $v(t)$ by differentiating $s(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}s}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2{t}^{3}-9{t}^{2}+3t-2) \\\\  & =6{t}^{2}-18t+3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we differentiate $v(t)$ to find $a(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(6{t}^{2}-18t+3) \\\\  & =12t-18\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we put $a=0$ to find the time when the acceleration is zero:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}12t-18 & =0 \\\\ t & =\\frac{18}{12} \\\\ t & =\\frac{3}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the acceleration is zero when $t=\\frac{3}{2}.$ To find the velocity at this moment, we substitute this back into $v(t)$ to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(\\frac{3}{2}) & =6{(\\frac{3}{2})}^{2}-18(\\frac{3}{2})+3 \\\\  & =6(\\frac{9}{4})-27+3 \\\\  & =\\frac{27}{2}-27+3 \\\\  & =-\\frac{21}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-109302/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "bee6d4bf-79da-5eb3-a214-8c045dbce5bd"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-109302"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-335906/field-1/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer/id #uuid "b799486a-3a34-5012-8eb2-40d2060c035a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-335906/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "9883c0c2-64e6-59f0-a592-6d80b6d75371" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-335906/field-1/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer-field/choices ["q-335906/field-1/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-335906/field-2/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0" :answer/id #uuid "46b58199-f9d9-567b-bfaf-99cd1a368168" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-335906/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "38e1fde2-d1f3-5faa-8af2-8a854a4a24d0" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-335906/field-2/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0" :answer-field/choices ["q-335906/field-2/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-335906" :question/id #uuid "a057f4ca-b8df-55b8-b000-d7d91fd329b9" :question/math-academy-id "q-335906" :question/problem "A particle $P$ is traveling along the $x$-axis with displacement $s(t)$ from a fixed origin $O$ given by\n\n$$\ns(t)={t}^{5}+5t,\\,t\\ge 0.\n$$\n\nFind the time at which the acceleration is zero, and find the value of the velocity at this moment.\n\nThe acceleration is zero at $t=$\n{{field-1}}, and the velocity at this moment is\n$v=$\n{{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "First, we calculate $v(t)$ by differentiating $s(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}s}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{5}+5t) \\\\  & =5{t}^{4}+5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we differentiate $v(t)$ to find $a(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(5{t}^{4}+5) \\\\  & =20{t}^{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we put $a(t)=0$ to find the time when the acceleration is zero:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}20{t}^{3} & =0 \\\\ {t}^{3} & =0 \\\\ t & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the acceleration is zero when $t=0.$ To find the velocity at this moment, we substitute this back into $v(t)$ to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(0) & =5(0)^{4}+5 \\\\  & =0+5 \\\\  & =5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the acceleration is zero at $t=0,$ and the velocity at this moment is $v=5.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-335906/field-1" "q-335906/field-2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "bee6d4bf-79da-5eb3-a214-8c045dbce5bd"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-335906"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-213"] :question/problem "The position $s(t)$ of a particle (in meters) at time $t$ seconds is given by \n\n$$\ns(t) = -\\frac{1}{3}t^3 + \\frac{5}{2}t^2 + 6t + 1,\\quad t\\geq 0.\n$$\n\nCalculate the time at which the particle is stationary, and give the displacement of the particle from the origin at this time." :question/worked-solution "The particle is stationary when its velocity is zero. So first, we need to calculate the velocity function. We can do that by taking the derivative of the position function, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}s}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(-\\frac{1}{3}{t}^{3}+\\frac{5}{2}{t}^{2}+6t+1) \\\\  & =-{t}^{2}+5t+6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe particle is stationary when $v=0\\, \\textrm{m/s}$. So, we set $v = 0$ and solve for $t \\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}0 & =-{t}^{2}+5t+6 \\\\ 0 & ={t}^{2}-5t-6 \\\\ 0 & =(t-6)(t+1)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe solutions are $t=6$ and $t=-1.$ Since $t\\geq 0,$ we discard the solution $t=-1$ and keep only $t=6.$\n\nSo the particle is stationary only at $t=6\\, \\textrm{s}.$ To find the displacement from the origin at this time, we substitute $t=6$ back into $s(t)$ and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}s(6) & =-\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot {6}^{3}+\\frac{5}{2}\\cdot {6}^{2}+6\\cdot 6+1 \\\\  & =-72+90+36+1 \\\\  & =55\\,\\text{m}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the particle is stationary at $t = 6\\, \\textrm{s}$ and its displacement from the origin at this time is $55\\, \\textrm{m}.$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-6159"] :question/problem "The displacement $s,$ in meters, relative to a fixed origin $O$ of a particle moving in a straight line along the $x$-axis is given by $s(t) = t^4 - 32t$, where $t \\geq 0$ is the time measured in seconds. Determine the time intervals in which the particle is moving in the direction of decreasing $x.$" :question/worked-solution "If the particle moves in the direction of decreasing $x,$ then its velocity is negative. \n\nFirst, we calculate the velocity function by differentiating the position function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}s}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{4}-32t) \\\\  & =4{t}^{3}-32\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo calculate time intervals in which the particle is moving in the direction of decreasing $x$, we solve the inequality $v(t) <    0\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & <0 \\\\ 4{t}^{3}-32 & <0 \\\\ 4{t}^{3} & <32 \\\\ {t}^{3} & <8 \\\\ t & <2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the time interval in which the particle is moving to the direction of decreasing $x$ is $t\\in\\left[ 0, 2\\right).$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-217"] :question/problem "A particle $P$ is traveling along the $x$-axis with displacement $s(t)$ from a fixed origin $O$ given by\n\n$$\ns(t) = t^3-3t^2+12t,\\quad t\\geq 0.\n$$\n\nFind the time at which the acceleration is zero, and find the value of the velocity at this moment." :question/worked-solution "First, we calculate $v(t)$ by differentiating $s(t)$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}s}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{3}-3{t}^{2}+12t) \\\\  & =3{t}^{2}-6t+12\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nNow, we differentiate $v(t)$ to find $a(t)$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3{t}^{2}-6t+12) \\\\  & =6t-6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we put $a=0$ to find the time when the acceleration is zero:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}0 & =6t-6 \\\\ 6t & =6 \\\\ t & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo the acceleration is zero when $t=1$. To find the velocity at this moment, we substitute this back into $v(t)$ to get\n\n$$\nv(1) = 3(1)^2 - 6(1)+12 = 9.\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]}]
